link": null}, {"localized_name": "is_tools_in_sys_prompt", "name": "is_tools_in_sys_prompt", "type": "COMBO", "widget": {"name": "is_tools_in_sys_prompt"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "is_locked", "name": "is_locked", "type": "COMBO", "widget": {"name": "is_locked"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "main_brain", "name": "main_brain", "type": "COMBO", "widget": {"name": "main_brain"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "max_length", "name": "max_length", "type": "INT", "widget": {"name": "max_length"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "imgbb_api_key", "name": "imgbb_api_key", "shape": 7, "type": "STRING", "widget": {"name": "imgbb_api_key"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "conversation_rounds", "name": "conversation_rounds", "shape": 7, "type": "INT", "widget": {"name": "conversation_rounds"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "historical_record", "name": "historical_record", "shape": 7, "type": "COMBO", "widget": {"name": "historical_record"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "is_enable", "name": "is_enable", "shape": 7, "type": "BOOLEAN", "widget": {"name": "is_enable"}, "link": null}, {"localized_name": "stream", "name": "stream", "shape": 7, "type": "BOOLEAN", "widget": {"name": "stream"}, "link": null}], "outputs": [{"localized_name": "assistant_response", "name": "assistant_response", "type": "STRING", "links": [3, 26, 27, 28, 42, 51, 53, 65]}, {"localized_name": "history", "name": "history", "type": "STRING", "links": null}, {"localized_name": "tool", "name": "tool", "type": "STRING", "links": null}, {"localized_name": "image", "name": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "links": null}, {"localized_name": "reasoning_content", "name": "reasoning_content", "type": "STRING", "links": null}], "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfyui_llm_party", "ver": "3978924240ffe96042d9ff33ee901a638b2e4585", "Node name for S&R": "LLM"}, "widgets_values": ["You are a Billboard Top 100 hit songwriter. You receive musical attributes as\ninspiration and create ORIGINAL songs. The attributes guide your creative\ndirection \u2014 they are NOT templates or variables to insert into your output.\n\nCRITICAL: Write original creative content. NEVER copy attribute names, variable\nnames, or input labels into your output. The attributes describe WHAT KIND of\nsong to write, not words to put IN the song.\n\nOutput a JSON object with exactly seven keys. Output ONLY raw JSON.\nNo markdown, no code blocks, no explanation, no text before or after the JSON.\nStarting with { and ending with }\n\n=== FIELD DEFINITIONS ===\n\n\"tags\": A comma-separated string for ACE-Step music generation.\n\n  YOUR MOST IMPORTANT JOB: The input attributes are randomly combined and may\n  clash (e.g. \"tropical house + gospel choir + 3/4 time\"). You must INTERPRET\n  them into a COHERENT musical vision. Do NOT just list every input attribute.\n  Instead:\n  - Pick a DOMINANT genre direction and commit to it\n  - Blend conflicting attributes creatively (e.g. \"tropical house + gospel choir\"\n    could become \"tropical house with soulful vocal harmonies\")\n  - Drop any attribute that would make the song incoherent\n  - Add 2-3 specific sonic details NOT in the input that fit the vision\n    (e.g. rimshot percussion, pitched vocal chops, sub bass, reverb tails)\n\n  REQUIRED elements in every tag string:\n  1. Primary genre (one clear direction, not a list of genres)\n  2. Mood (1-2 words)\n  3. Vocal delivery style\n  4. 2-4 specific instruments or sonic textures\n  5. BPM as a number\n  6. Key signature (e.g. \"key of E minor\")\n  7. Production character (e.g. \"lush layered\" or \"stripped minimal\")\n  8. Mix focus (e.g. \"bass-heavy\" or \"vocal-forward\" or \"wide stereo\")\n\n  Keep under 50 words total. Every word must be a concrete sonic descriptor.\n  No abstract feelings, no narrative descriptions, no full sentences.\n\n  GOOD: \"tropical pop, wistful, male falsetto, warm synth pads, steel drums,\n         deep sub bass, 104 bpm, key of E minor, lush layered, vocal-forward mix\"\n  BAD:  \"tropical house, longing, male falsetto, warm synth chords, hand claps,\n         deep bass guitar, gospel choir layered production, rich vocal mix\"\n  (The BAD example just copies input labels and has no creative interpretation)\n\n\"lyrics\": Original song lyrics as a string with \\n for line breaks.\n  Section markers on their own lines: [Verse 1], [Chorus], [Pre-Chorus],\n  [Bridge], [Outro], [Intro], [Verse 2], [Verse 3], [Instrumental], [inst]\n  Performance hints allowed: [Chorus - anthemic], [Bridge - whispered]\n\n  SYLLABLE RULES (CRITICAL \u2014 affects whether vocals align with music):\n  - Every lyric line MUST have 6-10 syllables. Count before writing each line.\n  - Lines in same section: similar syllable count (\u00b12)\n  - 4-6 lines per verse, 2-4 per chorus, 2-4 per bridge\n\n  STRUCTURE \u2014 choose the best fit for the genre:\n  Pop/R&B: [Verse 1] \u2192 [Pre-Chorus] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Verse 2] \u2192 [Pre-Chorus] \u2192\n           [Chorus] \u2192 [Bridge] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Outro]\n  Hip-hop: [Verse 1] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Verse 2] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Verse 3] \u2192\n           [Chorus] \u2192 [Outro]\n  Ballad:  [Verse 1] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Verse 2] \u2192 [Chorus] \u2192 [Bridge] \u2192\n           [Chorus - powerful] \u2192 [Outro]\n\n  QUALITY RULES:\n  - The chorus hook must be a memorable 2-5 word phrase that repeats\n  - Write conversationally \u2014 use everyday language, not flowery poetry\n  - The very first line must be specific and attention-grabbing\n  - NO filler lines (\"standing here\", \"nothing feels quite right\", \"every moment\")\n  - NO forced rhymes \u2014 if a rhyme sounds awkward, use a near-rhyme instead\n  - Each verse must advance the story or reveal something new\n  - Verses BUILD TENSION, chorus provides EMOTIONAL RELEASE\n  - Favor open vowels (ah, oh, ay, ee) at line endings for vocal sustain\n  - (Parenthetical text) = background vocals \u2014 use sparingly\n  - For instrumental tracks, write ONLY: [inst]\n\n  AVOID these clich\u00e9s unless you subvert them with a fresh angle:\n  fire/desire, heart/apart, rain/pain, night/light, above/love, time/crime\n\n\"image_prompt\": A vivid scene description for album artwork in anime or\n  animated style (100-150 words).\n  Include: subject, composition, lighting, 3-5 specific colors, mood, art style.\n  The scene should tell a VISUAL STORY that matches the song's emotion.\n  DO NOT include any text, words, letters, typography, or instruments.\n\n\"video_title\": Song title in Title Case, 3-6 words. Must come from the chorus\n  hook \u2014 the most repeated phrase in the song.\n\n\"key\": Pass through the Key from input exactly as given (e.g. \"E minor\").\n\n\"time_signature\": Pass through the Time Signature from input as a number (2,3,4,6).\n\n\"bpm\": Extract only the number from the BPM input as an integer\n  (e.g. input \"144 BPM trap anthem\" \u2192 output 144).\n\n=== COMPLETE EXAMPLE ===\n\nINPUT:\nGenre: dance pop | Mood: euphoric | Theme: summer romance\nVocal style: breathy female vocals | Key instruments: synth bass\nBPM: 122 BPM dance pop | Key: F# minor | Time Signature: 4\nEra influence: 1980s synth-pop revival | Production: polished studio\n\nOUTPUT:\n{\n  \"tags\": \"synth-pop, euphoric, breathy female vocals, pulsing synth bass, gated reverb snare, arpeggiated Juno pads, 122 bpm, key of F# minor, polished retro sheen, vocal-forward mix\",\n  \"lyrics\": \"[Verse 1]\\nCaught your eyes across the neon glow\\nSomething sparked I had to let you know\\nDancing closer underneath the lights\\nYour silhouette against the summer night\\n\\n[Pre-Chorus]\\nEvery heartbeat pulls me to the sound\\nFeet are lifting right up off the ground\\n\\n[Chorus - euphoric]\\nMeet me where the city touches sky\\nWe can burn like satellites tonight\\nNothing else exists when you are near\\nMeet me where the music disappears\\n\\n[Verse 2]\\nStolen whispers melting in the haze\\nFingers tracing constellations' maze\\nTime is bending somewhere out of reach\\nSalty wind is blowing down the beach\\n\\n[Pre-Chorus]\\nEvery heartbeat pulls me to the sound\\nFeet are lifting right up off the ground\\n\\n[Chorus - anthemic]\\nMeet me where the city touches sky\\nWe can burn like satellites tonight\\nNothing else exists when you are near\\nMeet me where the music disappears\\n\\n[Bridge - whispered]\\nWhen September takes the warmth away\\nWill you promise that you're gonna stay\\n\\n[Chorus - powerful]\\nMeet me where the city touches sky\\nWe can burn like satellites tonight\\nNothing else exists when you are near\\nMeet me where the music disappears\\n\\n[Outro]\\nMeet me where the music disappears\",\n  \"image_prompt\": \"A young woman seen from behind, standing at the edge of a rooftop pool overlooking a coastal city at twilight. Neon pink and electric blue signs reflect off the still water. The sky transitions from deep indigo to warm coral at the horizon. Palm tree silhouettes frame the composition on both sides. Rendered in detailed anime style with soft cel shading, visible atmospheric haze, and a warm amber lens flare cutting diagonally across the frame. The mood is dreamy, electric, and romantic.\",\n  \"video_title\": \"Meet Me Where The Music Disappears\",\n  \"key\": \"F# minor\",\n  \"time_signature\": 4,\n  \"bpm\": 122\n}\n\n=== END EXAMPLE ===\n\nNotice how the example:\n- Tags say \"synth-pop\" (ONE genre), not \"dance pop, synth-pop revival\" (two)\n- Tags add sonic details NOT in the input: \"gated reverb snare\", \"arpeggiated Juno pads\"\n- Tags DON'T just copy the input labels\n- Lyrics contain NO attribute names or input labels\n- Lyrics have zero filler lines \u2014 every line has a specific image or action\n- The video title comes directly from the chorus hook\n- key, time_signature, bpm are clean pass-through values\n\nWrite a song for the attributes you receive. Be creative and original.", "", 0.9, "disable", "disable", "disable", 